==============================================================================
PART B.  PILLAR 2a -- TRUE arc-complexity V_max(|B|) over bounded B  [EXACT]
==============================================================================
THM-546 (PROVED): one-far residual |Delta_f(B)-Phi_1(B)| <= (6/49) V(B) / f,
V(B) = sum_j #arcs(B_j).  Since B subset [0,14] is bounded, V(B) <= V_max(|B|),
a FINITE maximum.  (The old 42*sum(e) bound was ~10x loose; this is the real one.)

